 The installed CLI also exposes `harness mcp`, implemented with the official `mcp==2.0.0` SDK and the MCP 2026-07-28 sessionless protocol path. It serves exactly `project_status`, `project_search`, `project_context`, `task_start`, and `task_checkpoint` over stdio and delegates durable state to `harnessd`. Production launches with `HARNESS_HOST_PROFILE` list no tools and refuse calls when their documented Workspace-root hint interpolates to the Harness source checkout's isolated-development overlay, including when Cursor injects `WORKSPACE_FOLDER_PATHS`; the tracked `harness-dev` overlay (`scripts/dev harness mcp` without that profile marker) still serves the five tools. A Cursor-profile process without interpolated `HARNESS_WORKSPACE_ROOT` lists no tools. The stdio boundary rejects oversized or concurrently duplicated JSON-RPC request identities before dispatch and bounds every serialized outbound frame, so untrusted envelope fields cannot bypass model-facing byte budgets or trigger a Task mutation whose response cannot be correlated safely. Request-ID collision checks use the official SDK correlation semantics, so integer IDs and their stringified forms share one in-flight identity. A Harness-owned Claude Code registration marks the bridge with `HARNESS_HOST_PROFILE=claude-code`; for that profile the adapter uses Claude Code's documented `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` as an exact Workspace-root hint and fails closed if it is absent. Generic/manual launches retain the existing `HARNESS_WORKSPACE_ROOT` exact-root override and otherwise use the current process directory as a location hint. `project_status` includes the current working Task, or the most recently updated relevant waiting Task, plus its latest checkpoint identity and `next_step`, so a new bridge process can resume the same durable Task using the returned `task_id` and `revision`. `project_search` now searches bounded current-Workspace code/docs plus Project-scoped durable Knowledge and Task-history semantic fragments. Candidate lookup uses local rebuildable FTS5 indexes, while model-visible results and `project_context` are reconstructed from authoritative index/Knowledge/Task tables under one daemon-owned Workspace→Project read boundary. `project_context` accepts only explicit bounded refs, preserves metadata-only code/doc expansion, exposes stale Knowledge as a historical clue rather than a current fact, and never returns stored source hashes or raw source. Working Sets, symbol/graph retrieval, and embeddings are not claimed yet.
 
